    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tanētum</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tannētum</span></b> , i, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a village of Upper
				Italy</i>, now <i>Taneto</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 21,
			25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">21, 26</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">30,
			19</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tannētāni</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tanē-</span></b> ),
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Tanetum</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 15,
				20, § 116</span></i>.</div>
